         exact-payload byte counter, its cover-size floor, its JPEG save/share copy, and the
         check's measured sturdy caption (task W2-4, spec.md gate-30). New v6 copy for this
         screen only; kept in its own file (not strings.xml) so parallel v6 tasks don't collide
         on one shared resource file. The exact-technique's existing copy is untouched. -->

    <!-- Technique selector (mirrors AudioStegoScreen's "technique" section/row style). -->
    <string name="workshop_image_technique_label">technique</string>
    <string name="workshop_image_technique_exact">exact</string>
    <string name="workshop_image_technique_sturdy">sturdy</string>

    <!-- v6 (task W2-7): sturdy's payload SLOT is a fixed size (SturdyImageCarrier.PAYLOAD_BYTES =
         64), but the real message length is now variable, 1..64 (the frame's own length field
         carries it, zero-padding the rest of the slot), so sturdy shares exact's plain
         "%1$d / %2$d bytes" live counter (ImageStegoScreen.kt) and no longer needs its own
         exact-byte-count strings. -->

    <!-- General actions caption (task #28's original), sturdy variant: the exact-technique
         string this replaces always writes PNG, which is no longer true once sturdy writes
         JPEG; see save/share below. -->
    <string name="workshop_image_actions_caption_sturdy">embed hides text in the image, extract reads it back, check scans for hidden data without extracting it. save/share unlock after a successful embed and write JPEG here, since that\'s what sturdy is built to survive.</string>

    <!-- gate-30: the check's caption when technique = sturdy, written from the measurement in
         SturdyImageSteganalysisRealPhotoTest.kt: on real photos this check's flagged/clear
         reading tracks the photo's own JPEG pattern, not whether anything is hidden, and mostly
         stops flagging anything at all once a photo is actually sent. -->
    <string name="workshop_image_check_caption_sturdy">this check looks for exact\'s last-bit changes, not sturdy\'s brightness-cell shifts. in a small test on real photos it flagged sturdy output exactly as often as the same photos untouched, and after a real send it rarely flagged either, so flagged or clear here says little about sturdy.</string>

    <!-- Save/share: sturdy always writes a JPEG (Pictures/Nightjar, image/jpeg) so the hidden
         data survives; exact's own "saved to your photo gallery as PNG" string is unchanged. -->
    <string name="workshop_image_saved_jpeg">saved to your photo gallery as JPEG</string>
    <string name="workshop_image_save_action_jpeg">save as JPEG</string>
</resources>
